Set-up
Give the app registration a name that names this Umbral instance (for example "Umbral — home"): Microsoft shows it to people when they first sign in.
REDIRECT URI TO REGISTER WITH THE PROVIDER
Copy
A Microsoft client secret expires: after 6 months by default, 24 months at most. Note the date. Once it has passed, nobody can sign in through Microsoft until you replace the secret here.

Who can sign in: personal Microsoft accounts, with any email domain.

Settings
DISPLAY NAME

Shown on the sign-in button as "Sign in with …" and on the admin screens.

APPLICATION (CLIENT) ID

On the app's Overview page in the Microsoft Entra admin center.

CLIENT SECRET
••••••••6789
REPLACE THE CLIENT SECRET

Leave blank to keep the saved secret. A new one is the secret's Value, not its Secret ID.

WHO MAY SIGN IN
Personal Microsoft accounts
Outlook.com, Hotmail, Xbox and Skype accounts. In the registration: Personal accounts only.
Work or school accounts from one organization
The people of one Microsoft Entra tenant, given by its tenant ID below. In the registration: Single tenant only.
Any work or school account
People from any organization that uses Microsoft Entra. In the registration: Multiple Entra ID tenants.
Personal and any work or school account
Both of the above. In the registration: Any Entra ID Tenant + Personal Microsoft accounts.
DIRECTORY (TENANT) ID

The organization's tenant ID, a GUID. Used only with "Work or school accounts from one organization".

Shared with every app

Shared connectors are offered to every app set to "all shared connectors". Untick it to offer this one only to the apps that choose it.

ALLOWED EMAIL DOMAINS

Only people whose verified email is at one of these domains can sign in through this connector. Leave empty to use the instance list (none: anyone can sign in).

To limit one app, create a connector for it with the domain rule and offer only that connector to the app.

